    "s1": { "x": 2350, "y": 1530, "w": 380, "fill": "gray", "text": "First run\nOne question per screen with a sanity line under the answer (Neo).\nA 5-step checklist instead of a long form (Neo).\nCreating a wallet is a small ceremony (Apple Wallet's Adding Card).\nDelight here is fine: it happens once (Family's delight curve)." },
    "s2": { "x": 3290, "y": 2784, "w": 380, "fill": "gray", "text": "Daily loop\nHome is your wallets as a stack of real-looking cards (Apple Wallet).\nThe eye hides every amount, for the BTS (Neo private mode).\nAdding happens in trays over Home, each a different height, one action each (Family).\nPhotos: take one or pick from the album in its own short tray; Bun can read a slip if you let it.\nSave = one tick, one haptic, and the record flies into its card. No confetti on a daily action." },
    "s3": { "x": 1410, "y": 4038, "w": 380, "fill": "gray", "text": "Understand\nRecord detail: the amount large, then plain facts (Apple Wallet).\nInsights: month bars, then categories, with an info tray for every number (Neo).\nRecap: the one place for confetti, plus how many records GoGoCash might pay back on, opt-in only (Neo rewards recap)." },
    "s10": { "x": 5170, "y": 12816, "w": 380, "fill": "gray", "text": "Slip auto-import\nThe phone decides what is a slip (QR check); other photos never leave it.\nImages are read and dropped; only fields and a salted reference hash stay.\nOpen: auto-save mode (recommend out of v1), daily reading default (recommend off), a backfill allowance beyond 10 slips a day." },
    "s11": { "x": 4230, "y": 14070, "w": 380, "fill": "gray", "text": "Travel\nRecords keep their own amount, currency, the rate used and the home amount frozen at save.\nExchanging cash is one record with both amounts, not spending.\nOpen: rate provider; trip spending counts in the month budget as designed." },
    "s12": { "x": 5640, "y": 15324, "w": 380, "fill": "gray", "text": "System states\nEvery failure says records are safe and offers another way.\nOpen: when signed out from another phone, keep unsent records (this design) or discard them (sign-out tray)? Where does contact support lead?" },
    "s14": { "x": 3760, "y": 17832, "w": 380, "fill": "gray", "text": "Dark tokens\nGround #0E0D12, card #1A1920, sheet #24222B, text #F4F2FA, quiet #A9A6B6, violet text #B9A3F9, under #4CC38A, over #F47C93.\nMaterials deepen; titanium gets a 1 px edge. Primary button and + flip to light." }
  },
